{
  "schema": "transport/accounting-literal-oracle/1",
  "independence": "These expected statuses and reasons are literal author decisions frozen before implementation. A fixture builder may serialize/hash/clone declared input data, but must never compute expected outcomes from implementation logic.",
  "fixture_rules": {
    "canonicalization": "Every materialized plan, artifact and ledger is canonical JSON per the contract. Hash plan first, substitute PLAN_SHA256 into artifacts, hash artifacts and set exact ledger artifacts, then hash ledger. Supply those held roots separately. No expected status is generated by this process.",
    "base": "Use plan below, artifact E1 below, and one RECORDED ledger record per slot referencing its measurement. Records have reason empty. Artifact declaration IDs, sizes and digests are computed only from the literal supplied artifact bytes.",
    "edits": "Apply listed edits in order to named input objects. paths are literal object keys/array indices, not executable expressions. append adds the literal value; replace sets it; remove deletes it. Repin all resulting bytes in root order unless a case explicitly says retain_old_pins. These are fixture-data preparation instructions, not validation logic.",
    "copy_attempt": "A case may supply explicit extra attempt objects and new slot and measurement IDs. Copy the ten base slots in the SAME listed order, replace attempt and IDs with supplied literal lists, and copy measurements replacing IDs,slot and the explicitly supplied interval starts/ends. No implicit outcome or retry status is derived. This expands literal fixture data only.",
    "ledger_edits": "Default ledger remains exactly all materialized RECORDED slot references unless case edits change it. UNKNOWN requires removal of that slot's evidence measurement so no unused evidence remains. Removing an artifact's last measurement also removes that artifact and binding.",
    "expected_output": "assert expected status or refusal reason literally; for non-refusal also assert the listed invariants. Tests must not recalculate expected statuses using validator branches."
  },
